From 67f3aaaa1eba41da1090656bbebffe996193b054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:15:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 19/26] ling: CUDA graphs and RoCE gathers on by default
 (TF_LING_GRAPHS=0 / TF_LING_ROCE=0 turn them off): graphs dropped after every
 prompt chunk and whenever an eager forward is wider than any window since the
 last drop, since main's shared scratch may grow and move (a served run hit an
 illegal address on a stale graph); a wider window runs eager first so scratch
 never grows inside a capture. Gates: ling-tp every row's logits and drafts
 byte-equal graphs+RoCE vs eager NCCL (windows of 4 at 4,000 and across the
 4,096-key/8-chunk edge, MTP chains of 5); served fixed texts equal to the
 eager build's, drafted == plain on all four

---
 zig/src/families/ling/engine.zig |  7 +++---
 zig/src/families/ling/steps.zig  | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 zig/src/families/ling/tp.zig     |  6 ++---
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zig/src/families/ling/engine.zig b/zig/src/families/ling/engine.zig
